# REDIR-1 (BRAND-R2 — docs/BRAND_R_RUNBOOK.md §3b): the retired domain 301s to
# the primary, path for path, indefinitely.
#
# This file has to sit in public/. The Netlify Next.js runtime copies public/
# verbatim into the publish directory at build time; a _redirects in the repo
# root or written straight into .next is ignored (.next is emptied on build).
#
# Absolute `from` URLs scope each rule to one host, so readyhall.com, deploy
# previews and api.ukedl.com (Render, not this site) are untouched. The `!`
# forces the rule ahead of Next.js routing — without it, any path that still
# resolves on the old origin would be served there instead of redirecting.
# Netlify carries the query string across on its own.
#
# Requires ukedl.com + www to stay attached to the Netlify site as aliases, and
# readyhall.com to be the primary domain. With ukedl.com still primary, these
# fight Netlify's own alias-to-primary 301 and the pair loops.

https://ukedl.com/*      https://readyhall.com/:splat  301!
https://www.ukedl.com/*  https://readyhall.com/:splat  301!

